[0m[2mLooking[0m[2m at the original[0m[2m code[0m[2m more[0m[2m carefully, I[0m[2m see it[0m[2m checks[0m[2m stock[0m[2m, charges[0m[2m the[0m[2m customer[0m[2m, then decre[0m[2mments inventory[0m[2m. If decrement[0m[2m fails[0m[2m after[0m[2m charging[0m[2m, the customer[0m[2m gets[0m[2m charged[0m[2m but never[0m[2m receives[0m[2m the[0m[2m item—that[0m[2m's[0m[2m the[0m[2m bug. My[0m[2m approach[0m[2m adds[0m[2m a[0m[2m lock around[0m[2m the stock check and[0m[2m decrement[0m[2m to[0m[2m make them[0m[2m atomic[0m[2m, then[0m[2m releases[0m[2m inventory[0m[2m if payment[0m[2m doesn't[0m[2m go[0m[2m through[0m[2m.
     
